Scope file mount cache per user to prevent cross-user data exposure.

Under long-running PHP runtimes (FrankenPHP worker mode, RoadRunner,
ReactPHP, ...) cache.runtime survives across requests. The
backendUserAuthenticationFileMountRecords cache key has no user
parameterization, so user A's file mounts are served to user B.

Include the user UID in the cache key so each backend user gets
their own cached file mount set. Under PHP-FPM nothing changes
(the runtime cache dies with the process).

--- a/Classes/Authentication/BackendUserAuthentication.php
+++ b/Classes/Authentication/BackendUserAuthentication.php
@@ -1330,7 +1330,10 @@
     public function getFileMountRecords()
     {
         $runtimeCache = GeneralUtility::makeInstance(CacheManager::class)->getCache('runtime');
-        $fileMountRecordCache = $runtimeCache->get('backendUserAuthenticationFileMountRecords') ?: [];
+        // Include user UID in the cache key to prevent cross-user data
+        // exposure when the runtime cache survives across requests.
+        $cacheKey = 'backendUserAuthenticationFileMountRecords-' . (int)($this->user['uid'] ?? 0);
+        $fileMountRecordCache = $runtimeCache->get($cacheKey) ?: [];
 
         if (!empty($fileMountRecordCache)) {
             return $fileMountRecordCache;
@@ -1471,7 +1474,7 @@
             }
         }
 
-        $runtimeCache->set('backendUserAuthenticationFileMountRecords', $fileMountRecordCache);
+        $runtimeCache->set($cacheKey, $fileMountRecordCache);
         return $fileMountRecordCache;
     }
 
